From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: msiexec, msi: a package for all users is installed as an administrator

David: PuTTY installed but added no icons. msiexec ran a package installed
for all users as the user, who may not write to Program Files or
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE -- PuTTY's installer rolled back at "put the install
directory on the PATH". And msi put an all-users package's shortcuts in the
installing account's own Start menu (an upstream FIXME): installed elevated,
SYSTEM's, which nobody sees.

msiexec now runs itself again with "runas" -- the consent prompt, as Windows
asks -- when the package is for all users (ALLUSERS=1, or 2 without
MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1, and not marked as needing no elevation) and it is not
elevated; and msi points ProgramMenuFolder, StartMenuFolder, StartupFolder,
DesktopFolder, TemplateFolder, AdminToolsFolder and AppDataFolder at the All
Users profile when ALLUSERS=1.

Gate: make test-msiallusers (a perMachine package built with wixl). QA VM:
PuTTY 0.85 installs after the consent prompt and is in Start.
--- a/dlls/msi/package.c
